{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And you shall sound the shofar of teru'ah.</b> There is a dispute whether the world was created in Nisan or in Tishrei, and there is no need to elaborate, for the transmitters of the religion established for us in the prayers of Rosh HaShanah: 'This day is the beginning of Your handiwork, a remembrance of the first day.' Now, we see the sounding of the shofar in the Jubilee year in Tishrei, at the beginning of the year. And furthermore, regarding the assembly of the people to read the Torah on the festival of Sukkot, it is written 'so that they hear and so that they learn,' and it is not possible for this to be after half the year (and furthermore 'and the festival of ingathering at the going out of the year,' and likewise 'the turning of the year'). And the trustworthy witness is the sabbatical year, concerning which it is written 'you shall not sow,' and in Marheshvan they begin in the land of Israel to sow. Now if the beginning of the year were from Nisan, they would not reap what they sowed in the sixth year, nor would they sow, for behold it is the sabbatical year; and since they would not reap the seed of the sixth year, they would not sow twice, and Scripture says 'you shall not sow' in the seventh year alone. And Judah the Persian said that Israel reckoned by the solar calculation, and had this been correct, Moses would not have explained 'the course of a full year,' for the astrologers were unable until now to bring it to light: for the sages of India add a fifth of an hour onto the quarter-day, and Ptolemy and his associates say that a three-hundredth part of a day is lacking, and it is closer than the course of the intercalation, and those who came after him said a 106th part, and after that 110th, and after that 130th, also 180th, for there is one whose year for the completion of the zodiac is from a visible point, and there is from the point of the oblique sphere to the right and to the left, and we need the tradition. And furthermore, the meaning of 'month' will refute the Persian. And the Sadducees say that the religion is based on the lunar year. Know that the moon has no year at all; rather, the calculators sought a number of months close to the solar year and found twelve, just as the sun has no month. And the calculators sought a number for the month that would be divisible close to the month of the days of the lunar months, because our months are lunar, and our years ultimately return to solar years. Therefore our Sages of blessed memory transmitted that the court would always make seven intercalations in every cycle — a halakhah given to Moses at Sinai — even though they would fix each month according to the sighting of the moon. And the secret of the cycle is known from the science of the stars:" "And the meaning of <b>ta'viru</b> is that they sound the shofar throughout the constellations."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The text of the second parenthetical '(במ״ט אינו)' is obscure; rendered hyper-literally in sequence. It may be a corrupted insertion or marginal notation. Also, several manuscripts vary in the exact fractional figures cited for different astronomers' solar-year estimates."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:12:29.112277257Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}